     <p>
         <b>NutritionIntake:</b> This resource is used to document the intake of foods, drinks, oral nutrition supplements, and other consumables like infant formula or breastmilk. It records patient consumption—whether past, present, or planned—based on inputs from the patient, family members, or healthcare providers. 
-        See <a href="https://build.fhir.org/nutritionintake-examples.html">Nutrition Intake Examples</a>
+        Examples: <a href="nutritionintake-examples.html">NutritionIntake Examples</a>.
     </p>
 
     <p>
         <b>NutritionProduct:</b> Focuses on identifying consumable food products, both solid and liquid, intended for human consumption. This includes general food items, beverages, and other nutritional consumables used in patient care settings. 
-        See <a href="https://build.fhir.org/nutritionproduct-examples.html">Nutrition Product Examples</a>
+        Examples: <a href="nutritionproduct-examples.html">NutritionProduct Examples</a>.
     </p>
 
     <p>
         <b>NutritionOrder:</b> This resource describes various dietary requests made for patients. It includes general oral diets (e.g., General Healthy diet), therapeutic diets (e.g., low-sodium or fluid-restricted diets), oral nutrition supplements, enteral feedings (tube feeding), and infant formulas. 
-        See <a href="https://build.fhir.org/nutritionorder-examples.html">Nutrition Order Examples</a>
+        Examples: <a href="nutritionorder-examples.html">NutritionOrder Examples</a>.
     </p>
 
